5. No rate limiting on auth endpoints\
server.js:89,123 \'97 /api/auth/register and /api/auth/login have zero rate limiting, enabling brute-force, credential stuffing, and bcrypt-DoS.\
Fix: Add express-rate-limit on auth routes (e.g., 5 req/min per IP).\
\
6. Regex injection (ReDoS) in search\
server.js:198-201 \'97 User-supplied q passed directly to $regex. Crafted patterns like (a+)+$ cause catastrophic backtracking.\
Fix: Escape special regex chars:\
\
const escapeRegex = (s) => s.replace(/[.*+?^$\{\}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&');\
7. No email format validation on registration\
server.js:95 \'97 Only checks presence (!email), not format. Any string including " " is accepted.\
Fix: Add regex or library validation for email format.\
\
8. No password strength enforcement\
server.js:95, models/User.js:8 \'97 A single-character password is accepted.\
Fix: Enforce minimum length (e.g., 8 chars) and basic complexity.\
